---
import Landing from "../../layouts/Landing.astro";
import Footer from "../../features/navigation/components/Footer.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../features/navigation/components/SiteHeader.astro";

const locale = "en";
---

<Landing locale={locale} title="Terms of Service — Qably" description="Terms of use for Qably, the platform that organizes test cases and receives the results of your CI.">
  <SiteHeader locale={locale} altHref="/terms" />

  {/* Main Terms Content */}
  <main id="main-content" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pt-28 pb-16 flex-grow font-sans text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed space-y-12">
    <header class="space-y-3 pb-8 border-b border-white/[0.08]">
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider font-medium">Last updated: October 20, 2026</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="text-base text-zinc-400">
        Terms of use for Qably, the platform that organizes test cases and receives the results of your CI.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">1. Service description</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
        The service covers the intake of CI results (JUnit XML reports sent to the API with an API key, through <code class="text-white font-mono bg-zinc-900 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">POST /runs/ingest/junit</code> or <code class="text-white font-mono bg-zinc-900 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded">POST /runs/ingest</code>), flaky test signals, and AI-assisted case documentation. Proposals for new cases require approval by a person. Qably does not run tests: each customer's CI runs them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">2. Organizations, roles and API keys</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
        API access is managed with API keys that belong to a project and that only an owner or an admin can create and revoke. The roles in an organization are <code class="text-zinc-300">owner</code>, <code class="text-zinc-300">admin</code>, and <code class="text-zinc-300">member</code>. The customer is responsible for safeguarding its API keys and for assigning the roles in its organization. Actions performed with a valid API key are considered authorized by the account-holding organization.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">3. Ownership of customer code</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
        The customer keeps ownership of its source code, specifications, and test results. Qably <strong>claims no ownership rights</strong> over them. The Privacy Policy details which data is sent to external services.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">4. Limits and fair use</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
        Each plan sets limits on members, projects, and Aeris credits; the API applies request limits per minute. Qably may revoke API credentials in response to intentional attempts to overload or abuse the API.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer locale={locale} />
</Landing>
